---
id: RS-006
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: catch-all serde flatten without validation
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 6

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(attribute_item (attribute (identifier) @attr arguments: (token_tree) @serde_args)) @target'

related: [RS-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

A `#[serde(flatten)]` catch-all map on a `Deserialize` struct accepts unknown
input keys into an extension bag. That can be deliberate, but the validation
boundary must be visible: validate the extras, use `#[serde(try_from = "...")]`,
put a `deserialize_with` validator on the field, or suppress with a reason when
forward-compatible extension keys are intentional and validated elsewhere.

This rule is **opt-in** and only targets catch-all map shapes such as
`HashMap<String, serde_json::Value>` / `BTreeMap<String, serde_json::Value>`.
Typed flatten composition (`common: CommonConfig`) is out of scope.
